# No em dashes

Never write the em dash character (U+2014) in UI copy, code comments, docs,
commit messages, LLM prompts, or chat replies.

Use a comma, colon, period, or parentheses instead. For an empty table cell or
missing value, use `-`.

```tsx
// BAD
description="Preview first — deletes cannot be undone."
{row.company || '\u2014'}

// GOOD
description="Preview first. Deletes cannot be undone."
{row.company || '-'}
```

Exceptions: code that must recognise em dashes in incoming text (résumé
parsing, title normalisation) writes them as the `\u2014` escape, never as the
literal character.

Enforced by `frontend/src/test/noEmDash.test.ts`, and every LLM call gets the
same rule through `STYLE_RULE` in `app/core/llm_client.py`.
